  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Mainly dry for today, though daily chances \nfor showers and thunderstorms return on Monday.\n\nOne area of strong storms just southwest of Somerset Co. \nThese should pass to the south of our area, but cold front\nwell to the northwest still. Models bring in lower dewpt\nair into central PA later today, so will go with the dry\nmodel solution for now, but would not be surprise something\npops up today.\n\nAs the airmass dries out a bit this afternoon, temperatures \nwill likely be warmer than in past days.\n\nWarm and more humid airmass works back into the area on \nMonday, given rise to more showers and storms. \n\nAt this point, looks like the main chance for strong storms\nand heavy rain would be mainly to the southwest, more like\nOhio into WV. NAM lowers dewpoints again on Tuesday, \nsupporting more in the way of dry weather after early Tue. \n\nCooler for late week, but with weak systems moving southeast\nin a northwest flow pattern, could still be wet at times.",
